From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WiVRn Android port <noreply@invalid>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] aux/android: include <vector> for std::vector usage

org.freedesktop.monado.auxiliary.hpp uses std::vector<float> but never
includes <vector> itself, relying on it being pulled in transitively
by something else. That happens to work with some libc++ versions but
not others -- surfaced building against NDK 29's libc++ (worked fine
against NDK r28b). Fix the missing include directly rather than
depending on transitive header inclusion.
---
 src/xrt/auxiliary/android/org.freedesktop.monado.auxiliary.hpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/xrt/auxiliary/android/org.freedesktop.monado.auxiliary.hpp b/src/xrt/auxiliary/android/org.freedesktop.monado.auxiliary.hpp
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/src/xrt/auxiliary/android/org.freedesktop.monado.auxiliary.hpp
+++ b/src/xrt/auxiliary/android/org.freedesktop.monado.auxiliary.hpp
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@

 #include "wrap/ObjectWrapperBase.h"

+#include <vector>
+
 namespace wrap {
 namespace android::app {
 	class Activity;
--
2.55.0
